We need a class that implements the ITriggerableEvent interface.

-- Solution:
```ts
class SingleEventTarget<T> implements ITriggerableEvent<T> {
  private handlers: ((data: T) => void)[] = [];

  on(handler: (data: T) => void): void {
    this.handlers.push(handler);
  }

  off(handler: (data: T) => void): void {
    this.handlers = this.handlers.filter((h) => h !== handler);
  }

  trigger(data: T): void {
    this.handlers.forEach((h) => h(data));
  }
}
```

-- Explanation:
This class implements the ITriggerableEvent interface. It has a private field called handlers that stores an array of handlers.

